On the contrary.  I've created some levels and inserted them into the main
dungeon script at level 2, without having to change the source code.  Time
and patience were necessary, but that was for figuring out the grammar of
the level compiler listed in the man page and learning some of its quirks.
It took me a while to get an honest to goodness shop created, with shopkeeper
and merchandise and everything, for example.  But using the mine def script
as a guide helps a lot.

